  "stem": "A pattern of square tiles is built in stages. The number of tiles in stage \\(n\\) is given by \\(T(n) = n^{2} + 2n\\). How many tiles are in stage 9?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "99"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Substitute \\(9\\) for \\(n\\): \\(T(9) = 9^{2} + 2(9)\\).",
    "\\(81 + 18 = 99\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "n = symbols('n')\nT = Lambda(n, n**2 + 2*n)\nassert T(9) == 99\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [T(9)]",
